WEBVTT

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.360
Hanno Ginza

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.030
Man, I wanna go someplace nice and cool!

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.360
We could pop into a store.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.560
No, I mean a mountain!

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.740
What'll we climb next?

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.540
Mountains are nice and cool!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.490
Hanno Station

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.730
Yeah...

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:43.490
What's wrong?

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.750
I made Mom worry an awful lot 
when we went to Mt. Fuji,

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.280
so it's a little hard for me to tell 
her I'm going to the mountains again.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.610
Oh, yeah...

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.510
In that case, how about 
we invite your mom along?

00:01:58.970 --> 00:01:59.720
Mountain Trail

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.470
Season 2 - New Climb 14

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.970
Season 2 - New Climb 14 
Mt. Kirigamine With Mom!

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.720
Always Treasure Our Beautiful Nature!
City of Forest Culture, Hanno

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.720
Hello, Dad?

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.960
I'm wondering, is there a perfect mountain

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.520
we could visit with Aoi's mom along?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.650
How does Kirigamine sound?

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.350
<i>Kirigamine?</i>

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.230
<i>Isn't that a brand of air conditioner?</i>

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:21.490
No, no, it's also a mountain in Nagano.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.120
The place is suitable for beginners, 
without any really dangerous areas.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.620
It's a lovely and refreshing mountain.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.990
Okay, then we'll go there!

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.980
<i>I'm just finishing up work here.{not in script}</i>

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.610
<i>Shall we take our car?{not in script}</i>

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.320
Sure! Thanks!

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.020
Dad said he'll drive!

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.390
Don't make plans like that without my input!

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.360
No biggie, I'm sure it'll be fun!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.550
Ask your mom what day's good for her.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.270
Okay.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.890
Say, Mom...

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.050
Yes?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.680
Hinata invited me to go to Mt. Kirigamine.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.080
Kirigamine?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.210
She said it's a mountain in Nagano.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.030
I'm pretty sure it's nice and cool there.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.090
Do you want to come with us, Mom?

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.130
Oh, but you don't have to!

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.690
I see...

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.180
Then I'll join you.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.340
Great! Let's go!

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.500
This really takes me back!

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.810
I haven't been to the mountains since college.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.710
What should I wear?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.630
I believe regular clothes will be fine,

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.360
but you should bring a jacket just in case.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.780
Even in summer, it gets cool in the mountains.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.400
Also, I think athletic shoes would be best.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.740
That makes sense.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.360
You really know your stuff, Aoi.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.600
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.710
<i>Mom's excited to go!</i>

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:53.870
<i>And so...</i>

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.400
<i>the day came for us to go visit Kirigamine.</i>

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>What sort of mountain is it?</i>

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.010
<i>Will Mom enjoy it?</i>

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.010
Look!

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.530
So many flowers!

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.020
They're very pretty.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.440
Say, Dad, which one's Kirigamine?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.870
"Which one"?

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:18.770
This entire plateau is called Kirigamine.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.030
Teach us, Kaede-san!! Segment

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.200
Teach us, Kaede-san!

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.030
<i>Bow...</i>

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.400
Mt. Kirigamine, with an 
elevation of 1925 meters

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.860
and located south of the 
Yatsugatake Mountain Range,

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.410
is a beautiful mountain included in the 
list of Japan's Hundred Famous Mountains.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.570
It has good transportation access,

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:38.270
and the low difference in elevation 
between the trail start and the summit

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:44.360
makes climbing easy for beginners, to the 
point where it could be considered hiking.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.080
Today, our goal is the summit 
of Mt. Kuruma over there.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.370
What's that round thing up top?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.640
A weather radar station.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.940
It is pretty close.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.900
Wait, is that a lift?!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.110
N-No way!

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:05.010
Ah, right... You do have 
trouble with high places.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.940
But don't worry, we won't 
be taking the lift today.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:15.370
Kirigamine Mountain Range

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:15.370
Mt. Kuruma 
Summit

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.570
While the lift would get us to the 
summit right away, that's no fun.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.370
Instead, we'll hike up 
around the area like this.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:18.560
Th-Thank goodness...

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:23.260
It's nice and cool!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.160
Yeah, it feels great!

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.240
Well, shall we get going?

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.890
Heading out!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.520
We're descending a hill 
while climbing a mountain...

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.850
Won't we have to climb 
that much higher later on?

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.840
Are you all right, Mom?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.140
We'll take it slow, without overdoing it.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:48.860
Since Kirigamine means "Fog Ridge", 
doesn't it get foggy here?

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.310
Right. Though the weather's nice today,

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:54.790
there are times when it's covered 
in fog, as the name implies.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:06:00.790
At those times, apparently they ring the bell 
at Mushoutou Tower to help indicate direction.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.050
Entrance Gate

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.350
It says it's a deer-proof fence.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.530
It's an entrance for people and vehicles.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:19.730
A deer!

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:20.850
Where? Where?!

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.980
Aww, it left already.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.030
Man!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.780
Shinanoji Nature Trails - Chushin Highlands Route
Mt. Kuruma Shoulder 1.8 km

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.120
Such tranquil scenery...

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.340
It's like you can see forever.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:34.910
Yeah!

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.500
Dragonflies!

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.340
You're right!

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:40.170
Wow!

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.550
The seasons really differ between 
the mountains and the town!

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.380
Wow!

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.640
<i>I've seen something like this before...</i>

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.770
<i>I know! It was the mountain 
Hinata and I climbed as kids!</i>

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.780
<i>Which mountain was that?</i>

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.700
Say, Hinata...

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:14.990
Where was that mountain we climbed 
when we were kids, again?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.380
You don't remember?!

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.280
Sorry...

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:20.050
Sheesh, you're such a disappointment, Aoi!

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.160
You see, that mountain was...

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:22.970
Yeah?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.480
Uh, I don't remember either! Sorry!

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.900
Hey!

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.880
Hm, where was it?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:37.140
I kinda remember it had tall grass and 
dragonflies flying around, like this.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.690
That's right.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.730
It was a lot like this.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.330
Those girls really walk fast.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.190
It's because they climb often.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.320
They've built up their stamina.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:57.770
When Aoi came back all worn-out from Mt. Fuji,

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:00.000
I wondered about her.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.260
There's nothing much to worry about.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:09.340
By preparing properly in advance and 
avoiding bad weather and difficult places...

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:14.560
in short, by not overdoing it... 
accidents will rarely happen.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.350
That does make sense.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.310
Such lovely scenery!

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.020
I had no idea there was scenery like this.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.570
So this is what she was wanting to see.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.340
<i>Walking on her own two feet,</i>

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:34.230
<i>she's steadily experiencing 
scenery that I haven't.</i>

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.570
<i>And steadily becoming an adult.</i>

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.360
<i>It makes me happy...</i>

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.580
<i>but also a little sad.</i>

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.230
Hey!

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.080
Mom!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.540
Well, shall we eat? You must be hungry.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.500
Watchtower Stone
Shiozawa

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:51.500
All right!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.260
Peep Ramen

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.260
Here, help yourselves!

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.890
Thanks for the food!

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.330
It's so good!

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.980
Food must taste better than 
usual when eaten on a mountain.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.800
No, it really is delicious, honest!

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.380
I made this too!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.880
To avoid having leftover soup,

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:19.200
the trick is to cut up ingredients in 
advance and cook with less water!

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:22.140
Who goes to the mountains for instant ramen?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:27.500
It combines the four best qualities: 
high-calorie, easy, light, and cheap.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.540
It's exceptional when you're exhausted.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:35.890
It's good!

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.720
It really is good!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.670
I'll have more!

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.470
Hey, no fair!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.460
We'll head out once you're done eating.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.460
So good!

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.270
Let me have me some!

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:44.120
Hey, are you listening?

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.270
No, it's mine!

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.450
Over there is the summit.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.860
Just a bit further.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.560
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.240
<i>Hinata's dad might remember.</i>

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.510
Um, uh...

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.450
That's right!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:02.870
Say, Dad, what was that mountain 
that Aoi and I climbed as kids?

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.540
<i>She beat me to it...</i>

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:07.420
Oh, that was Mt. Tanigawa.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:08.960
Mt. Tanigawa...

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:14.460
<i>That's the mountain Kaede-san 
recommended earlier.</i>

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.230
Now that you mention it, you did go there.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.570
While in the interior of Gunma Prefecture,

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:24.470
it's one of the few mountains where climbing
 trails start in walking distance of a station.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.490
There's a ropeway partway there.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.730
A ropeway?!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.850
Oh, right. Kaede-san mentioned that too.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:35.180
Aoi, you used to be fine with high 
places when you were little...

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:41.240
Apart from the more serious routes, 
Mt. Tanigawa is fairly safe to climb.{it actually has several very dangerous & steep & avalanche-prone routes up; they'd be taking the gently-sloped path that's safe, especially during warmer months}{it actually has the highest fatality of any mountain on earth, more so than Everest! mostly rock-climbing routes or attempts at new routes, but still...}

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.090
Yeah, considering how we could climb it as kids.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:47.250
It has nice mountain huts too.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.500
Mt. Kuruma Summit
1925 meters

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.250
We're here!

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.810
What lovely scenery!

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.430
Mom, are you tired?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.060
Yes, but it's a good tired.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.690
Thanks for inviting me.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.060
I'm glad I came!

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.960
Though I'll probably have 
sore muscles tomorrow...

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.230
Mt. Tanigawa, huh...

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:27.910
Yeah.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:31.160
<i>That's the mountain of our memories.</i>

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:35.000
<i>The scenery that I saw long ago with Hinata...</i>

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.770
<i>I want to see it again.</i>

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.960
<i>Can we go there?</i>

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:42.800
What?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.590
Oh, nothing!

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.810
Aoi! That settles which mountain we'll climb next!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.560
Yeah!

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:56.230
<i>Though I'm afraid of the ropeway, 
we'll aim for Mt. Tanigawa!</i>

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued!

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:00.150
{ED}
